1. **A method for binaural synthesis using a wearable audio device, the method comprising:**  

   receiving an audio signal representing at least one virtual sound source having an intended spatial direction relative to a listener;  

   generating, from the audio signal, a plurality of directional audio signals based on the intended spatial direction;  

   processing at least a portion of the directional audio signals within a frequency range of 4 kHz to 12 kHz to encode binaural directional information;  

   distributing the processed directional audio signals among at least four physical sound sources carried by the wearable audio device, including at least two physical sound sources positioned at different locations around a left ear of the listener and at least two physical sound sources positioned at different locations around a right ear of the listener; and  

   driving the at least four physical sound sources to emit respective acoustic signals toward corresponding pinnae of the listener such that the respective acoustic signals interact with different portions of the corresponding pinnae before entering ear canals of the listener, thereby producing direction-dependent pinna filtering and causing the at least one virtual sound source to be perceived as originating from the intended spatial direction.
